From: Jason Rhinelander <jason@imaginary.ca>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 18:21:49 -0300
Subject: Include session/router.hpp for complete tunnel_info

Older libstdc++ (Debian bullseye g++-10, Ubuntu jammy g++-11) requires
session::router::tunnel_info to be a complete type for the std::unordered_map
member in SessionRouter; include its definition instead of relying on the
forward declaration. Newer toolchains (bookworm/noble+) accept the forward
declaration, so this is only needed on those two distros.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 include/session/network/routing/session_router_router.hpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/session/network/routing/session_router_router.hpp b/include/session/network/routing/session_router_router.hpp
index 805b734..cde409e 100644
--- a/include/session/network/routing/session_router_router.hpp
+++ b/include/session/network/routing/session_router_router.hpp
@@ -9,6 +9,10 @@
 #include <unordered_map>
 #include <vector>
 
+// Older libstdc++ (bullseye/jammy) needs tunnel_info complete for the std::unordered_map
+// member below, so pull in its full definition rather than only forward-declaring it.
+#include <session/router.hpp>
+
 #include "session/network/backends/session_file_server.hpp"
 #include "session/network/request_queue.hpp"
 #include "session/network/routing/network_router.hpp"
